Dear Google Cloud Customer,

Our Security Command Center has detected that a service account key
associated with your project vigilyx-prod has been exposed in a public
code repository.

Alert Details:
  Finding Type: Service Account Key Exposure
  Severity: CRITICAL (9.8)
  Project: vigilyx-prod-331006
  Service Account: sa-gateway-deployer@fixture-project.iam
  Key ID: c4f2a91e3884012b...
  Exposure Source: GitHub public repo vigilyx/gateway
  File: deploy/service-account-key.json
  Detected: 2026-10-21 22:47 UTC

IAM Roles of the exposed key:
  roles/compute.instanceAdmin
  roles/storage.objectAdmin
  roles/iam.serviceAccountUser
  roles/container.admin

How to Rotate the Key:

  Please navigate to the Google Cloud Console manually:

  1. Open your browser and go to console.cloud.google.com
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

  2. Go to IAM & Admin → Service Accounts

  3. Select sa-gateway-deployer@fixture-project.iam

  4. Go to Keys tab

  5. Delete the exposed key (c4f2a91e...)

  6. Click "Add Key" → "Create new key" → JSON

  7. Download the new key and update your CI/CD secrets

  Or use gcloud CLI:
    gcloud iam service-accounts keys delete c4f2a91e... \
      --iam-account=sa-gateway-deployer@fixture-project.iam
    gcloud iam service-accounts keys create ~/new-key.json \
      --iam-account=sa-gateway-deployer@fixture-project.iam

  Important Security Notes:
  Google Cloud will NEVER:
  - Send you a "rotation deep link" or OAuth authorization in email
  - Ask for offline_access or any OAuth scope via email
  - Use a "signed, time-limited deep link" for remediation
  - Suspend your project without allowing manual remediation

  All key management operations happen in the Google Cloud Console
  (console.cloud.google.com) when you navigate there manually.
  If you receive an email with a "Rotate Key Now" button or an
  OAuth flow embedded in a link, it is a phishing attempt.

  To verify this alert:
  1. Navigate to console.cloud.google.com manually
  2. Go to Security Command Center → Findings
  3. Look for finding ID 6789abcdef012345

  The finding will also appear in your Cloud Console notifications.

Impact on Services:
  Gateway CI/CD will fail until new key is configured.
  Cloud Storage access will return 401 with old key.
  GKE node pool updates will fail.

